  "note": "SYNTHETIC, NOT A SURVEY and never installed (underscore folder). The pand geometry (BAG/3DBAG) is De Clercqstraat 22-2 (clercq-236681) with the two corner pands re-read with their second street; the designs are an invented 1920s Amsterdam School shop row that exercises the five components of the Jan Evertsenstraat set: rigid continuous canopies (two continuity.canopy groups), ladder windows paired per bay, multi-bay erkers (hip and flat caps), brick course banding, and corner towers (a shared-vertex corner with a stepped cap, a chamfered corner with a pyramid cap)."
